  <documents xsi:type="kernel:StructuredDocument" id="dfeb2820-55e4-5f4b-8cac-38947622522a" name="Developer completion and demo boundary" format="MARKDOWN" content="Accept bounded export jobs and expose status/result separately from queued execution.&#10;Accept only after job and recoverable dispatch intent persist together; replay returns one job.&#10;Select at most 1000 rows from the immutable 10000-row snapshot; publish one correct private CSV per job.&#10;Cancellation commits only in QUEUED/RUNNING; if it wins workers cannot publish success, and if success wins cancellation conflicts.&#10;Only owners see status/cancel/download; CANCELLED jobs have no result. Configure five concurrent workers and recover partial batches.&#10;Generated function shells require real Go application code. Review endpoint reachability, resource permissions, contracts and naming before deployment." description="Reviewed demonstration model; not a deployment/acceptance certificate" />
